  "articleBody": "It's easy to look at a scuff or a small dent and think you can handle it yourself, but sometimes interior damage is more serious than it appears. You should really think about bringing in a professional when you're dealing with structural issues, like if that dent goes deeper than just the surface drywall. Also, if you've got stains that seem to have really set in, especially on something porous, it's probably time to call in someone with specialized tools and knowledge to get it truly gone. When the damage is on a specialized material, like a custom tile or a unique wood finish, trying a DIY fix could actually make it worse. And honestly, if you want the repair to be totally seamless and hard to detect – like it was never even there – a pro has the eye and the experience to blend it perfectly. They've got the know-how to match colors and textures, so you're not left with a patch that screams 'repair here!' If you're in the greater Denver area, give us a call; we can assess the damage and let you know the best way forward. Don't let a small issue turn into a bigger headache later on.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
